@startuml
!theme plain
title E-commerce Card Authorization — Synthetic End-to-End Sequence
actor Shopper
participant Merchant
participant "Payment Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Orchestrator" as Orch
participant "Acquirer / Switch" as Acquirer
participant "Card Network" as Network
participant Issuer
Shopper -> Merchant : checkout and confirm amount
Merchant -> Gateway : create intent (idempotency key, payment token)
Gateway -> Gateway : authenticate and validate request
Gateway -> Orch : authorize
Orch -> Orch : create intent and attempt
Orch -> Acquirer : authorization via processor adapter
Acquirer -> Network : mapped authorization request
Network -> Issuer : issuer authorization
Issuer --> Network : approval or decline
Network --> Acquirer : network result
Acquirer --> Orch : mapped response and references
alt Approved
  Orch -> Orch : mark authorized (not settled)
  Orch --> Gateway : approval and authorization reference
else Declined
  Orch -> Orch : record decline result
  Orch --> Gateway : decline and mapped reason
else Result unknown
  Orch -> Orch : state UNKNOWN, schedule recovery
  Orch --> Gateway : pending / ambiguous outcome
end
Gateway --> Merchant : payment intent outcome
Merchant --> Shopper : display status
note over Acquirer,Issuer
Specific ISO 8583 MTIs/data elements and 3DS authentication
depend on acquirer/network rules and are not specified here.
end note
@enduml